.Dd September 17, 2026
.Dt ARCSYNC 1
.Os Darwin
.Sh NAME
.Nm arcsync
.Nd archive a photo library to a hybrid CD/DVD ISO
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl nqv
.Op Fl -json
.Op Fl -force
.Op Fl -library Ar path | Fl -dir Ar path
.Op Fl -out Ar path
.Op Fl -media Ar cd Ns | Ns Ar dvd Ns | Ns Ar dvd-dl Ns | Ns Ar bd Ns | Ns Ar none
.Op Fl -split
.Op Fl -burn
.Op Fl -volume-name Ar name
.Op Fl -from Ar YYYY-MM-DD
.Op Fl -to Ar YYYY-MM-DD
.Op Fl -cloud Ar skip Ns | Ns Ar derivative Ns | Ns Ar fail
.Op Fl -edited
.Op Fl -thumb-size Ar px
.Op Fl -title Ar text
.Op Fl -include-hidden
.Op Fl -include-trashed
.Op Fl -help
.Op Fl -version
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
reads a macOS Photos library or a plain photo folder, copies the media into a
dated filesystem tree, builds a static HTML gallery, and wraps the result in a
hybrid CD/DVD/Blu-ray
.Pa .iso
via
.Xr hdiutil 1 .
With
.Fl -burn ,
it then runs
.Nm hdiutil burn
on that ISO.
.Pp
It is a small terminal tool: no GUI, no PhotoKit, no iCloud download inside the
binary. Originals are copied byte-for-byte when they are already on this Mac.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl -library Ar path
Photos library bundle
.Pq Pa .photoslibrary .
Default if neither
.Fl -library
nor
.Fl -dir
is given:
.Pa ~/Pictures/Photos\ Library.photoslibrary .
.It Fl -dir Ar path
Plain directory tree of images/videos instead of Photos.
Mutually exclusive with
.Fl -library .
Album pages follow the folder tree.
.It Fl -out Ar path
Output ISO path
.Pq default: Pa ./arcsync-YYYYMMDD.iso .
With
.Fl -split ,
this is the stem:
.Pa NAME-1.iso , NAME-2.iso , ... .
.It Fl -media Ar type
Capacity profile:
.Ar cd
(680 MiB),
.Ar dvd
(4300 MiB, default),
.Ar dvd-dl
(7900 MiB),
.Ar bd
(23000 MiB), or
.Ar none
(unlimited).
.It Fl -split
If the staged payload exceeds media capacity, emit multiple self-contained ISOs
instead of failing.
.It Fl -burn
After writing the ISO, burn it with
.Nm hdiutil burn
(optical drive required). The ISO file is kept.
.It Fl -volume-name Ar name
Disc volume label. Default
.Pa ARCSYNC_YYYYMMDD .
.It Fl -from Ar YYYY-MM-DD , Fl -to Ar YYYY-MM-DD
Inclusive capture-date filter (local civil date).
.It Fl -cloud Ar mode
What to do when a Photos original is not on disk:
.Ar fail
(default — refuse to write an ISO if anything selected is still only in iCloud),
.Ar skip
(copy only local originals; knowingly incomplete),
or
.Ar derivative
(fill holes with local previews; not an archive).
See
.Sx ICLOUD AND OPTIMIZED LIBRARIES .
.It Fl -edited
Prefer a local edited/rendered derivative when present.
.It Fl -thumb-size Ar px
Thumbnail long edge in pixels (96–640, default 240).
.It Fl -title Ar text
Gallery
.Li <title>
and H1 (default: volume name).
.It Fl -include-hidden
Include Photos Hidden album assets.
.It Fl -include-trashed
Include Recently Deleted.
.It Fl n , Fl -dry-run
Scan and print the plan; write nothing.
.It Fl v
Verbose: banner plus per-file copy lines on stderr.
.It Fl q
Quiet: errors and final summary only.
.It Fl -json
Final summary as one JSON object on stdout.
.It Fl -force
Overwrite an existing
.Fl -out
path.
.It Fl h , Fl -help
Print usage and exit 0.
.It Fl -version
Print the version banner (assembly souvenir) and exit 0.
.El
.Sh ICLOUD AND OPTIMIZED LIBRARIES
.Nm
copies files that are already on this Mac. It does not download from iCloud.
That is deliberate: a full original pull can take all night and needs Photos.app,
your Apple ID, and enough free disk. The tool will not pretend a preview is a
camera file.
.Pp
There are two usual setups.
.Ss Family and amateur libraries (iCloud Photos, Optimize Mac Storage)
Most rows in Photos are real. Most files under
.Pa originals/
are not. Photos keeps a small preview on the Mac and the camera original in
iCloud. Burning that library as-is gives you an index of names and a handful of
real files. Do not do that if you want an archive.
.Pp
Overnight pull, morning burn:
.Bl -enum
.It
Confirm free space. You need enough room for every original plus a little extra.
In Photos, open a photo and use Get Info if you need a feel for size, or run:
.Pp
.Dl arcsync -n
.Pp
The dry-run (with default
.Fl -cloud fail )
lists how many files are local originals and how many are not on
this Mac. If the missing/cloud-only count is large, free disk before the next
step.
.It
In Photos: Settings (or Preferences) → iCloud →
.Sy Download Originals to this Mac .
.It
Leave the Mac awake, plugged in, on the home network. Close the lid only if it
is set to stay awake on power. Photos will work through the library. This can
run for hours on a family library and overnight on a big one. A spinning
progress or a quiet Photos window is normal.
.It
In the morning, run the dry-run again:
.Pp
.Dl arcsync -n
.Pp
You want missing/cloud-only as close to zero as it will go. Shared Albums and
some screenshots may never land as originals; that is Photos, not
.Nm .
When fail would succeed (exit 0 on dry-run), burn:
.Pp
.Dl arcsync --media dvd --split --out ~/Desktop/family.iso
.Pp
.Fl -cloud fail
is the default for exactly this reason: if anything selected is still only in
the cloud,
.Nm
refuses to write an ISO rather than quietly omit pictures. A one-line
.Nm
with no flags will not silently burn an Optimize-Mac-Storage library.
.It
After the ISO is mounted and spot-checked, you may switch Photos back to
Optimize Mac Storage if you need the disk space. The disc is the archive;
iCloud can go back to previews. Do not delete the library until you have opened
.Pa index.html
on the disc and opened two or three full images from different years.
.El
.Ss Working photographers (originals already on a NAS, RAID, or folder)
If the camera files already live in a directory tree, skip Photos:
.Pp
.Dl arcsync --dir /Volumes/NAS/Jobs/2026 --media none --out job.iso
.Pp
If you use Photos only as a browser and the masters are elsewhere, point
.Fl -dir
at the masters. Album HTML will follow the folder tree. That is the 2000-era
workflow: the files were next to the machine because there was no cloud to hide
them in.
.Ss Fl -cloud skip and Fl -cloud derivative
.Fl -cloud skip
copies only local originals and skips anything still in iCloud.
Useful for a deliberate test burn of whatever happens to be local.
.Fl -cloud derivative
is intended to fill holes with local previews and mark those rows
.Li quality=derivative
in
.Pa manifest.tsv .
Treat that as a slideshow, not an archive. Family users who want the real files
should use
.Fl -cloud fail
after the overnight download, not derivative as a shortcut.
.Ss osxphotos
A third-party tool can ask Photos to fetch individual missing originals. It is
not part of
.Nm ,
it can crash Photos, and it needs extra permissions. Prefer the Download
Originals setting above unless you already know that tool.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It 0
Success (including dry-run).
.It 1
Usage / argument error.
.It 2
Library unreadable or schema unrecognized.
.It 3
No assets matched filters.
.It 4
Staging I/O error (disk full, permission, overwrite without
.Fl -force ) .
.It 5
Payload exceeds media capacity and
.Fl -split
was not set (or a single file is larger than the media).
.It 6
.Nm hdiutil
failed.
.It 7
Interrupted (SIGINT/SIGTERM).
.It 8
Cloud mode
.Ar fail
(the default) and at least one selected asset is not a local original.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa ~/Pictures/Photos Library.photoslibrary
Default Photos library.
.It Pa $TMPDIR/arcsync-<pid>/
Staging work root (removed on success).
.It Pa ./arcsync-YYYYMMDD.iso
Default output path.
.El
Terminal (or iTerm) may need Full Disk Access to read the Photos library
bundle. The tool cannot grant this for you.
.Sh DISC LAYOUT
.Bd -literal -offset indent
index.html                 landing page
open-me.html               alias of index.html
autorun.inf                Windows hint
README.txt                 how to open this disc
css/style.css
thumbs/                    generated JPEG thumbnails
albums/                    album / folder pages
media/YYYY/MM/DD/          real files (byte-for-byte)
by-date/index.html
missing.txt
manifest.tsv
.Ed
.Sh AUTORUN
True auto-open of HTML is not possible on modern macOS. The hybrid image uses
HFS open-folder so Finder shows the volume root, where
.Pa index.html
is obvious. On Windows,
.Pa autorun.inf
may prompt rather than auto-open; double-click
.Pa index.html
always works.
.Sh PHOTOS LIBRARY
The Photos
.Pa Photos.sqlite
schema is private and can change between major Photos versions. If the schema
is unrecognized,
.Nm
exits 2 with a clear error rather than crashing. Close Photos.app if the
database copy fails because of a lock.
.Sh EXAMPLES
See what is actually on this Mac before touching Photos settings:
.Pp
.Dl arcsync -n --cloud fail
.Pp
After originals have landed overnight:
.Pp
.Dl arcsync --media dvd --split --out ~/Desktop/family.iso
.Pp
Professional tree already on a NAS:
.Pp
.Dl arcsync --dir /Volumes/NAS/Masters --media none --out ~/Desktop/masters.iso
.Pp
Test burn of whatever happens to be local:
.Pp
.Dl arcsync --cloud skip --media none --out /tmp/test.iso
.Pp
Folder archive plus burn to optical media:
.Pp
.Dl arcsync --dir ~/Pictures/vacation --media dvd --burn --out ~/Desktop/vac.iso
